    {
        "user": "UKC0EQURX",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1755890284.274629",
        "client_msg_id": "e4cdafc7-f7d2-48fe-922a-11bb8c988cca",
        "text": "Love those ideas.\n<@U02LAK62DEV> Why this story matters: At a time when Chinatowns across the country are shrinking and struggling, San Francisco’s is seeing a revival. And it’s not driven by extractive business interests or a commercial repackaging of traditions — it’s being driven by young diasporic Chinese and Chinese American people who want to uplift and evolve cultural expression. Many of them were told growing up that they shouldn’t linger in Chinatown if they wanted a future in the U.S. Now they’re bringing that future to Chinatown.\n\n(Zhe, please correct as needed)",
        "team": "T036YAYMK",
        "user_team": "T036YAYMK",
        "source_team": "T036YAYMK",
        "user_profile": {
            "avatar_hash": "66e0f79cb2e7",
            "image_72": "https:\/\/avatars.slack-edge.com\/2024-08-13\/7572731157060_66e0f79cb2e729ba3691_72.jpg",
            "first_name": "Laura",
            "real_name": "Laura Wenus",
            "display_name": "Laura Wenus",
            "team": "T036YAYMK",
            "name": "laura.wenus",
            "is_restricted": false,
            "is_ultra_restricted": false
        },
        "thread_ts": "1755131189.960289",
        "parent_user_id": "U02LAK62DEV",
        "blocks": [
